table name to logs (as in "log_path.exe_name.pid").\x00' 0x2a0@0x155b5|0x15562=b'log_suffix\x00' 0x2a4@0x18504|0x184bd=b'String to append to log file name, e.g. ".txt".\x00' 0x2d4@0x1108b|0x1106d=b'log_to_syslog\x00' 0x2d8@0x17b8b|0x17b6b=b'Write all sanitizer output to syslog in addition to other means of logging.\x00' 0x308@0x11558|0x11534=b'verbosity\x00' 0x30c@0x1e5db|0x1e515=b'Verbosity level (0 - silent, 1 - a bit of output, 2+ - more output).\x00' 0x33c@0x193ec|0x19369=b'strip_env\x00' 0x340@0x12901|0x1291b=b'Whether to remove the sanitizer from DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES to avoid passing it to children on Apple platforms. Default is true.\x00' 0x370@0x142a6|0x14276=b'verify_interceptors\x00' 0x374@0x12981|0x1299b=b'Verify that interceptors are working on Apple platforms. Default is true.\x00' 0x3a4@0x17bd7|0x17bb7=b'detect_leaks\x00' 0x3a8@0x17be4|0x17bc4=b'Enable memory leak detection.\x00' 0x3d8@0x14da9|0x14d5c=b'leak_check_at_exit\x00' 0x3dc@0x142ba|0x1428a=b'Invoke leak checking in an atexit handler. Has no effect if detect_leaks=false, or if __lsan_do_leak_check() is called before the handler has a chance to run.\x00' 0x40c@0x170b5|0x170a4=b'allocator_may_return_null\x00' 0x410@0x12201|0x121cd=b'If false, the allocator will crash instead of returning 0 on out-of-memory.\x00' 0x440@0x1d783|0x1d6a9=b'print_summary\x00' 0x444@0x14359|0x14329=b'If false, disable printing error summaries in addition to error reports.\x00' 0x474@0x13b5d|0x13b32=b'print_module_map\x00' 0x478@0x1c747|0x1c63f=b"Print the process module map where supported (0 - don't print, 1 - print only once before process exits, 2 - print after each report).\x00" 0x4a8@0x1e620|0x1e55a=b'check_printf\x00' 0x4ac@0x1cec9|0x1cdf8=b'Check printf arguments.\x00' 0x4e4@0x16d13|0x16cd7=b'handle_segv\x00' 0x4e8@0x1ef71|0x1eea8=b"Controls custom tool's SIGSEGV handler (0 - do not registers the handler, 1 - register the handler and allow user to set own, 2 - registers the handler and block user from changing it). \x00" 0x518@0x1c7ce|0x1c6c6=b'handle_sigbus\x00' 0x51c@0x129cb|0x129e5=b"Controls custom tool's SIGBUS handler (0 - do not registers the handler, 1 - register the handler and allow user to set own, 2 - registers the handler and block user from changing it). \x00" 0x54c@0x15d0c|0x15ceb=b'handle_abort\x00' 0x550@0x1f69f|0x1f619=b"Controls custom tool's SIGABRT handler (0 - do not registers the handler, 1 - register the handler and allow user to set own, 2 - registers the handler and block user from changing it). \x00" 0x580@0x1f75a|0x1f6d4=b'handle_sigill\x00' 0x584@0x1ad37|0x1ac60=b"Controls custom tool's SIGILL handler (0 - do not registers the handler, 1 - register the handler and allow user to set own, 2 - registers the handler and block user from changing it). \x00" 0x5b4@0x1bf0a|0x1bdd9=b'handle_sigtrap\x00' 0x5b8@0x11878|0x11854=b"Controls custom tool's SIGTRAP handler (0 - do not registers the handler, 1 - register the handler and allow user to set own, 2 - registers the handler and block user from changing it). \x00" 0x5e8@0x1ffed|0x1ff67=b'handle_sigfpe\x00' 0x5ec@0x15d19|0x15cf8=b"Controls custom tool's SIGFPE handler (0 - do not registers the handler, 1 - register the handler and allow user to set own, 2 - registers the handler and block user from changing it). \x00" 0x61c@0x11099|0x1107b=b'allow_user_segv_handler\x00' 0x620@0x1f02c|0x1ef63=b'Deprecated. True has no effect, use handle_sigbus=1. If false, handle_*=1 will be upgraded to handle_*=2.\x00' 0x650@0x16538|0x164ec=b'use_sigaltstack\x00' 0x654@0x16d1f|0x16ce3=b'If set, uses alternate stack for signal handling.\x00' 0x684@0x11933|0x1190f=b'detect_deadlocks\x00' 0x688@0x143a2|0x14372=b'If set, deadlock detection is enabled.\x00' 0x6c0@0x19cb6|0x19c12=b'clear_shadow_mmap_threshold\x00' 0x6c4@0x1bf19|0x1bde8=b'Large shadow regions are zero-filled using mmap(NORESERVE) instead of memset(). This is the threshold size in bytes.\x00' 0x6f4@0x19cd2|0x19c2e=b'color\x00' 0x6f8@0x1dce5|0x1dc2f=b'Colorize reports: (always|never|auto).\x00' 0x728@0x1fffb|0x1ff75=b'legacy_pthread_cond\x00' 0x72c@0x1a37f|0x1a2cb=b'Enables support for dynamic libraries linked with libpthread 2.2.5.\x00' 0x75c@0x109c5|0x109b2=b'intercept_tls_get_addr\x00' 0x760@0x1339c|0x133af=b'Intercept __tls_get_addr.\x00' 0x790@0x1b150|0x1b049=b'help\x00' 0x794@0x1cee1|0x1ce10=b'Print the flag descriptions.\x00' 0x7c4@0x16d51|0x16d15=b'mmap_limit_mb\x00' 0x7c8@0x12a85|0x12a9f=b'Limit the amount of mmap-ed memory (excluding shadow) in Mb; not a user-facing flag, used mosly for testing the tools\x00' 0x7f8@0x133b6|0x133c9=b'hard_rss_limit_mb\x00' 0x7fc@0x193f6|0x19373=b'Hard RSS limit in Mb. If non-zero, a background thread is spawned at startup which periodically reads RSS and aborts the process if the limit is reached\x00' 0x82c@0x2000f|0x1ff89=b'soft_rss_limit_mb\x00' 0x830@0x1b6ef|0x1b5e8=b'Soft RSS limit in Mb. If non-zero, a background thread is spawned at startup which periodically reads RSS. If the limit is reached all subsequent malloc/new calls will fail or return NULL (depending on the value of allocator_may_return_null) until the RSS goes below the soft limit. This limit does not affect memory allocations other than malloc/new.\x00' 0x860@0x1e62d|0x1e567=b'max_allocation_size_mb\x00' 0x864@0x1948f|0x1940c=b'If non-zero, malloc/new calls larger than this size will return nullptr (or crash if allocator_may_return_null=false).\x00' 0x894@0x18534|0x184ed=b'heap_profile\x00' 0x898@0x110b1|0x11093=b'Experimental heap profiler, asan-only\x00' 0x8c8@0x1eb1c|0x1ea53=b'allocator_release_to_os_interval_ms\x00' 0x8cc@0x19506|0x19483=b'Only affects a 64-bit allocator. If set, tries to release unused memory to the OS, but not more often than this interval (in milliseconds). Negative values mean do not attempt to release memory to the OS.\n\x00' 0x8fc@0x143c9|0x14399=b'can_use_proc_maps_statm\x00' 0x900@0x133c8|0x133db=b'If false, do not attempt to read /proc/maps/statm. Mostly useful for testing sanitizers.\x00' 0x930@0x17849|0x17829=b'coverage\x00' 0x934@0x1bf8e|0x1be5d=b'If set, coverage information will be dumped at program shutdown (if the coverage instrumentation was enabled at compile time).\x00' 0x964@0x105ec|0x105f4=b'coverage_dir\x00' 0x968@0x195d4|0x19551=b'Target directory for coverage dumps. Defaults to the current directory.\x00' 0x998@0x15dd3|0x15db2=b'cov_8bit_counters_out\x00' 0x99c@0x18541|0x184fa=b'If non-empty, write 8bit counters to this file. \x00' 0x9cc@0x110d7|0x110b9=b'cov_pcs_out\x00' 0x9d0@0x14dbc|0x14d6f=b'If non-empty, write the coverage pc table to this file. \x00' 0xa00@0x1a3c3|0x1a30f=b'full_address_space\x00' 0xa04@0x1adf1|0x1ad1a=b'Sanitize complete address space; by default kernel area on 32-bit platforms will not be sanitized\x00' 0xa34@0x1f768|0x1f6e2=b'print_suppressions\x00' 0xa38@0x205b4|0x20523=b'Print matched suppressions at exit.\x00' 0xa68@0x14df5|0x14da8=b'disable_coredump\x00' 0xa6c@0x1f77b|0x1f6f5=b"Disable core dumping. By default, disable_coredump=1 on 64-bit to avoid dumping a 16T+ core file. Ignored on OSes that don't dump core by default and for sanitizers that don't reserve lots of virtual memory.\x00" 0xa9c@0x155c0|0x1556d=b'use_madv_dontdump\x00' 0xaa0@0x20021|0x1ff9b=b'If set, instructs kernel to not store the (huge) shadow in core file.\x00' 0xad0@0x1737a|0x17369=b'symbolize_inline_frames\x00' 0xad4@0x13421|0x13434=b'Print inlined frames in stacktraces. Defaults to true.\x00' 0xb04@0x13458|0x1346b=b'demangle\x00' 0xb08@0x13b6e|0x13b43=b'Print demangled symbols.\x00' 0xb38@0x1dd0c|0x1dc56=b'symbolize_vs_style\x00' 0xb3c@0x1e644|0x1e57e=b'Print file locations in Visual Studio style (e.g:  file(10,42): ...\x00' 0xb6c@0x110e3|0x110c5=b'dedup_token_length\x00' 0xb70@0x143e1|0x143b1=b"If positive, after printing a stack trace also print a short string token based on this number of frames that will simplify deduplication of the reports. Example: 'DEDUP_TOKEN: foo-bar-main'. Default is 0.\x00" 0xba0@0x11944|0x11920=b'stack_trace_format\x00' 0xba4@0x13461|0x13474=b'Format string used to render stack frames. See sanitizer_stacktrace_printer.h for the format description. Use DEFAULT to get default format.\x00' 0xbd4@0x1c7dc|0x1c6d4=b'compress_stack_depot\x00' 0xbd8@0x20067|0x1ffe1=b'Compress stack depot to save memory.\x00' 0xc08@0x19cd8|0x19c34=b'no_huge_pages_for_shadow\x00' 0xc0c@0x18572|0x1852b=b'If true, the shadow is not allowed to use huge pages. \x00' 0xc3c@0x1c00d|0x1bedc=b'strict_string_checks\x00' 0xc40@0x18d6c|0x18d0d=b'If set check that string arguments are properly null-terminated\x00' 0xc70@0x1961c|0x19599=b'intercept_strstr\x00' 0xc74@0x1e688|0x1e5c2=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for strstr and strcasestr functions to find more errors.\x00' 0xca4@0x17392|0x17381=b'intercept_strspn\x00' 0xca8@0x2008c|0x20006=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for strspn and strcspn function to find more errors.\x00' 0xcd8@0x1e6de|0x1e618=b'intercept_strtok\x00' 0xcdc@0x110f6|0x110d8=b'If set, uses a custom wrapper for the strtok function to find more errors.\x00' 0xd0c@0x1b84f|0x1b748=b'intercept_strpbrk\x00' 0xd10@0x1f84b|0x1f7c5=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for strpbrk function to find more errors.\x00' 0xd40@0x14e06|0x14db9=b'intercept_strcmp\x00' 0xd44@0x1b861|0x1b75a=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for strcmp functions to find more errors.\x00' 0xd74@0x1d791|0x1d6b7=b'intercept_strlen\x00' 0xd78@0x12afb|0x12b15=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for strlen and strnlen functions to find more errors.\x00' 0xda8@0x1c7f1|0x1c6e9=b'intercept_strndup\x00' 0xdac@0x1e6ef|0x1e629=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for strndup functions to find more errors.\x00' 0xddc@0x11141|0x11123=b'intercept_strchr\x00' 0xde0@0x155d2|0x1557f=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for strchr, strchrnul, and strrchr functions to find more errors.\x00' 0xe10@0x1cefe|0x1ce2d=b'intercept_memcmp\x00' 0xe14@0x1962d|0x195aa=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for memcmp function to find more errors.\x00' 0xe44@0x185a9|0x18562=b'strict_memcmp\x00' 0xe48@0x14e17|0x14dca=b'If true, assume that memcmp(p1, p2, n) always reads n bytes before comparing p1 and p2.\x00' 0xe78@0x1224d|0x12219=b'intercept_memmem\x00' 0xe7c@0x19cf1|0x19c4d=b'If set, uses a wrapper for memmem() to find more errors.\x00' 0xeac@0x200de|0x20058=b'intercept_intrin\x00' 0xeb0@0x134ee|0x13501=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for memset/memcpy/memmove intrinsics to find more errors.\x00' 0xee0@0x15de9|0x15dc8=b'intercept_stat\x00' 0xee4@0x1dd1f|0x1dc69=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for *stat functions to find more errors.\x00' 0xf14@0x15631|0x155de=b'intercept_send\x00' 0xf18@0x1c803|0x1c6fb=b'If set, uses custom wrappers for send* functions to find more errors.\x00' 0xf48@0x1e737|0x1e671=b'decorate_proc_maps\x00' 0xf4c@0x16d5f|0x16d23=b'If set, decorate sanitizer mappings in /proc/self/maps with user-readable names\x00' 0xf7c@0x1c022|0x1bef1=b'exitcode\x00' 0xf80@0x1e74a|0x1e684=b'Override the program exit status if the tool found an error\x00' 0xfb0@0x1c02b|0x1befa=b'abort_on_error\x00' 0xfb4@0x19673|0x195f0=b'If set, the tool calls abort() instead of _exit() after printing the error report.\x00' 0xfe4@0x12b4e|0x12b68=b'suppress_equal_pcs\x00' 0xfe8@0x12b61|0x12b7b=b'Deduplicate multiple reports for single source location in halt_on_error=false mode (asan only).\x00' 0x1018@0x1dd65|0x1dcaf=b'print_cmdline\x00' 0x101c@0x1f892|0x1f80c=b'Print command line on crash (asan only).\x00' 0x104c@0x15640|0x155ed=b'html_cov_report\x00' 0x1050@0x17c02|0x17be2=b'Generate html coverage report.\x00' 0x1080@0x1225e|0x1222a=b'sancov_path\x00' 0x1084@0x144af|0x1447f=b'Sancov tool location.\x00' 0x10b4@0x13b87|0x13b5c=b'dump_instruction_bytes\x00' 0x10b8@0x12bc2|0x12bdc=b'If true, dump 16 bytes starting at the instruction that caused SEGV\x00' 0x10e8@0x14e6f|0x14e22=b'dump_registers\x00' 0x10ec@0x196c6|0x19643=b'If true, dump values of CPU registers when SEGV happens. Only available on OS X for now.\x00' 0x111c@0x1a3d6|0x1a322=b'detect_write_exec\x00' 0x1120@0x1a3e8|0x1a334=b'If true, triggers warning when writable-executable pages requests are being made\x00' 0x1150@0x173a3|0x17392=b'test_only_emulate_no_memorymap\x00' 0x1154@0x1c849|0x1c741=b'TEST ONLY fail to read memory mappings to emulate sanitized "init"\x00' 0x1184@0x1226a|0x12236=b'test_only_replace_dlopen_main_program\x00' 0x1188@0x173c2|0x173b1=b'TEST ONLY replace dlopen(<main program>,...) with dlopen(NULL)\x00' 0x11b8@0x1f8bb|0x1f835=b'enable_symbolizer_markup\x00' 0x11bc@0x144c5|0x14495=b'Use sanitizer symbolizer markup, available on Linux and always set true for Fuchsia.\x00' 0x11ec@0x1e786|0x1e6c0=b'detect_invalid_join\x00' 0x11f0@0x17401|0x173f0=b'If set, check invalid joins of threads.\x00' 0x1234@0x1c719|0x1c611=b'include\x00' 0x1238@0x1c721|0x1c619=b'read more options from the given file\x00' 0x1260@0x14d97|0x14d4a=b'include_if_exists\x00' 0x1264@0x1dc8b|0x1dbd5=b'read more options from the given file (if it exists)\x00'
